<title>ZAIRE: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>ZAIRE GOVERNMENT LIST (970409)</p>
<p> ***********************************************************</p>
<p> *  9 Apr 97 - President Mobutu appointed General Likulia  *</p>
<p> *		 Bolongo emergency rule prime minister,	*</p>
<p> *		 replacing his arch foe Etienne Tshisekedi   *</p>
<p> *		 after less than a week.			   *</p>
<p> ***********************************************************</p>
<p> President...........(Marshal) MOBUTU Sese Seko</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p>Prime Minister (Apptd 9 Apr 97).....General Likulia BOLONGO**</p>
<p>							 (** See note above)</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p>OUTGOING GOVERNMENT (Sworn In 11 July 94,</p>
<p>Reshuffled 24 Dec 96):</p>
<p> Deputy Prime Minister...............General LUKULIA Bolongo**</p>
<p>    (Also Minister of Defence)	    (** Apptd PM 9 Apr 97)</p>
<p> Deputy Prime Minister.......KAMANDA Wa Kamanda</p>
<p>(Also Minister of Foreign Affairs)</p>
<p> Deputy Prime Minister...........MENDE Omalanga</p>
<p>(Also Minister of Transport &amp; Communications)</p>
<p> Deputy Prime Minister...........BANZA Mukalayi</p>
<p>(Also Minister of Mines)</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS:</p>
<p> Agriculture.......YEKI Bampende</p>
<p> Budget........BOLENGE Mokesombo</p>
<p> Civil Service....KASEREKA Kasai</p>
<p> Culture &amp; Arts..MBONZI Matayoko</p>
<p> Economy.........MAMBU ma Khenzu</p>
<p> Energy...........MANANGA Ditoka</p>
<p> Environment, Conservation, Tourism...TSHIBANDA Ntunda Mulongo</p>
<p> Finance...........Marco BANGULI</p>
<p> Foreign Affairs..See Deputy PMs</p>
<p> Foreign Trade......KITENGE Yezu</p>
<p> Health &amp; Family...KASONGO Numbi</p>
<p> Higher Education, Universities &amp;</p>
<p>    Scientific Research..........MUSHOBEKWA Kali Mba wa Katana</p>
<p> Information, Press................KOLONI Longo</p>
<p> Interior..........MWANDO Nsimba</p>
<p> International Cooperation...............Wivine NLANDU Kavindi</p>
<p> Justice, Institutional Reform &amp;</p>
<p> Lord Chancellor.....TSHIBWABWA Ashila Pashi</p>
<p> Labour.........BANDABASO Nadedo</p>
<p> Land Affairs..KAYUMBA Bin Amani</p>
<p> Mining...........See Deputy PMs</p>
<p> Planning........TABIANA Ngansia</p>
<p> Posts, Telephones, Telecommunications..........NYINDU Kitenge</p>
<p> Primary, Secondary &amp; Vocational Education.........EPEE Gambwa</p>
<p> Public Works.............Alexis THAMBWE Mwamba</p>
<p> Social Affairs.....BETU Kabamba</p>
<p> Sports, Youth &amp; Leisure....KISOMBE Kiaku Mwisi</p>
<p> State Investment Portfolio...............MBOSO Nkodia Mpwanga</p>
<p> Transport &amp; Communications......See Deputy PMs</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - -</p>
<p> Central Bank Governor...........Patrice DJAMBOLEKA Okitongono</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - -</p>
